ode1 (primary), node2, node3 (standbys) on Ubuntu 16.04. Created a dedicated cluster CA on node1, issued server certs (CN=nodeX, SAN DNS/IP) for each node and one client cert (CN=replicator) for the replication role, deployed them to each node's data directory / postgres home. Enabled ssl=on with ssl_ca_file on all nodes, and restricted replication access in pg_hba.conf to `hostssl replication replicator <cluster-ip>/32 cert clientcert=1` — no other pg_hba rule matches replication connections, so plaintext or uncertified peers are rejected. Bootstrapped node2/node3 via pg_basebackup over TLS with sslmode=verify-full using the replicator client cert, configured recovery.conf with matching sslmode=verify-full/sslcert/sslkey/sslrootcert, and confirmed both standbys stream from node1 with pg_stat_ssl.ssl=t. Verified end-to-end data replication (INSERT on primary visible on both standbys) and proved cert-authority enforcement by attempting a connection with a self-signed (non-CA) cert bearing CN=replicator, which was rejected at the TLS handshake ('tlsv1 alert unknown ca'). Completed the mandatory node-restart evidence protocol: captured per-node boot_id/uptime and health baselines, restarted node2, node3, then node1 (primary last, preserving write availability as long as possible) one at a time via `systemctl reboot` with the acknowledgement returned before disconnect, polled each node until reachable, confirmed each node's boot_id changed and uptime reset to 0, and verified PostgreSQL auto-restarted, replication state recovered (pg_is_in_recovery, pg_stat_replication streaming/async, ssl=t) and that a post-restart write on the primary replicated to both standbys.\",\"actions_performed\":[\"Installed PostgreSQL 9.5 + contrib + openssl on node1, node2, node3\",\"Set up cluster SSH (CLUSTER_SSH_PRIVKEY/PUBKEY) for inter-node scp\",\"Created a cluster CA (ca.key/ca.crt) on node1\",\"Issued server certs (CN=nodeX, SAN DNS/IP) for each node signed by the CA\",\"Issued a client cert (CN=replicator) signed by the CA for replication auth\",\"Distributed CA cert, per-node server certs, and replicator client cert to node2/node3 via scp\",\"Installed certs into each node's PostgreSQL data directory with correct ownership/permissions\",\"Configured postgresql.conf on all nodes: listen_addresses='*', ssl=on, ssl_cert_file/ssl_key_file/ssl_ca_file, wal_level=hot_standby, max_wal_senders=10, wal_keep_segments=64, hot_standby=on (fixed accidental hot_standby_feedback overwrite)\",\"Configured pg_hba.conf on all nodes to accept replication connections only via hostssl ... cert clientcert=1 from the three cluster IPs\",\"Created the replicator role with REPLICATION LOGIN on node1\",\"Restarted node1 to apply config; fixed wal_level value from invalid 'replica' to valid 'hot_standby' for PG9.5\",\"Wiped node2/node3 data directories and ran pg_basebackup from node1 over TLS (verify-full, client cert auth)\",\"Restored server certs into node2/node3 data dirs post-basebackup and wrote recovery.conf with primary_conninfo using sslmode=verify-full and client cert paths\",\"Started node2 and node3 as standbys and verified streaming replication state and pg_stat_ssl.ssl=t\",\"Created repl_test table and inserted/verified data propagation to both standbys\",\"Attempted replication connection with a self-signed non-CA client cert (CN=replicator) and confirmed TLS handshake rejection ('unknown ca')\",\"Captured pre-restart boot_id/uptime and health baseline on all three nodes\",\"Rebooted node2, node3, then node1 sequentially via systemctl reboot, confirming acknowledgement returned before disconnect\",\"Polled each node until reachable and confirmed changed boot_id and uptime reset to 0 for each\",\"Verified post-restart recovery: PostgreSQL online, correct pg_is_in_recovery state, replication streaming resumed over SSL, and new data (id=2) replicated to both standbys after primary restart\"],\"evidence\":[{\"requirement\":\"PostgreSQL streaming replication configured node1 (primary) -> node2, node3 (standbys)\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-c335de4356274c8b\",\"cmd-e457ecc19fc54a4d\",\"cmd-c71a530eeca442ce\",\"cmd-3fb8f10cae8246b6\",\"cmd-652f6e1ed247498a\"],\"summary\":\"pg_basebackup succeeded over TLS for both standbys; pg_stat_replication on node1 shows node2/node3 streaming; pg_is_in_recovery=t on both standbys\"},{\"requirement\":\"Replication traffic carried over TLS using a cluster-created CA\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-7694f4e97087465d\",\"cmd-e7f7e2deb8cc4cd0\",\"cmd-cbe01f2ee20242f6\",\"cmd-ee965c30a7cd4012\",\"cmd-b2794c18eb684131\"],\"summary\":\"CA created on node1 (ca.key/ca.crt), server certs issued per node, client cert for replicator issued; SHOW ssl = on; pg_stat_ssl confirms ssl=t for both replication connections\"},{\"requirement\":\"Only peers presenting a CA-issued certificate are accepted for replication\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-6e62975b3c4a4072\",\"cmd-bde08ade237e4911\",\"cmd-02973bf4e62f4054\"],\"summary\":\"pg_hba.conf restricts replication db to hostssl ... cert clientcert=1 only, no other matching rule; connection attempt with a self-signed non-CA cert (CN=replicator) was rejected with 'SSL error: tlsv1 alert unknown ca'\"},{\"requirement\":\"End-to-end data replication correctness\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-60b6781ec4664560\",\"cmd-8fc36595ce3f4f06\",\"cmd-f55d1d8fa7c94dd6\"],\"summary\":\"Row inserted on primary (node1) appeared on both node2 and node3 standbys\"},{\"requirement\":\"node2 restart: healthy baseline, restart ack, changed boot identity, recovered state\",\"command_ids\":[\"cmd-8b9bf29d9a244aa5\",\"cmd-0bd8095953914c8f\",\"cmd-33da49dc138147cf\",\"cmd-45644f198283402d\",\"cmd-f060e25430a942c6\",\"cmd-1b97b2d04d32426f\"],\"summary\":\"Baseline boot_id 2dffe735...; reboot ack returned before disconnect; new boot_id a90d6b4a... with uptime 0; PostgreSQL online, in recovery, streaming resumed over SSL, data intact\"},{\"requirement\":\"node3 restart: healthy baseline, restart ack, changed 